{"$message_type":"diagnostic","message":"cannot borrow `value` as mutable because it is also borrowed as immutable","code":{"code":"E0502","explanation":"A variable already borrowed with a certain mutability (either mutable or\nimmutable) was borrowed again with a different mutability.\n\nErroneous code example:\n\n```compile_fail,E0502\nfn bar(x: &mut i32) {}\nfn foo(a: &mut i32) {\n    let y = &a; // a is borrowed as immutable.\n    bar(a); // error: cannot borrow `*a` as mutable because `a` is also borrowed\n            //        as immutable\n    println!(\"{}\", y);\n}\n```\n\nTo fix this error, ensure that you don't have any other references to the\nvariable before trying to access it with a different mutability:\n\n```\nfn bar(x: &mut i32) {}\nfn foo(a: &mut i32) {\n    bar(a);\n    let y = &a; // ok!\n    println!(\"{}\", y);\n}\n```\n\nFor more information on Rust's ownership system, take a look at the\n[References & Borrowing][references-and-borrowing] section of the Book.\n\n[references-and-borrowing]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch04-02-references-and-borrowing.html\n"},"level":"error","spans":[{"file_name":"/Users/danluu/dev/rust-interp-semantic-reuse-20260913/experiments/proc-macro-arena-compiler-02/borrow_error.rs","byte_start":127,"byte_end":132,"line_start":4,"line_end":4,"column_start":29,"column_end":34,"is_primary":true,"text":[{"text":"    arena04_macros::mutate!(value);","highlight_start":29,"highlight_end":34}],"label":"mutable borrow occurs here","suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"expansion":null},{"file_name":"/Users/danluu/dev/rust-interp-semantic-reuse-20260913/experiments/proc-macro-arena-compiler-02/borrow_error.rs","byte_start":91,"byte_end":97,"line_start":3,"line_end":3,"column_start":16,"column_end":22,"is_primary":false,"text":[{"text":"    let held = &value;","highlight_start":16,"highlight_end":22}],"label":"immutable borrow occurs here","suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"ex